.SH NAME
Digest::base \- Digest base class
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&  package Digest::Foo;
\&  use base \*(AqDigest::base\*(Aq;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \f(CW\*(C`Digest::base\*(C'\fR class provide implementations of the methods
\&\f(CW\*(C`addfile\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`add_bits\*(C'\fR in terms of \f(CW\*(C`add\*(C'\fR, and of the methods
\&\f(CW\*(C`hexdigest\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`b64digest\*(C'\fR in terms of \f(CW\*(C`digest\*(C'\fR.
.PP
Digest implementations might want to inherit from this class to get
this implementations of the alternative \fIadd\fR and \fIdigest\fR methods.
A minimal subclass needs to implement the following methods by itself:
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    new
\&    clone
\&    add
\&    digest
.Ve
.PP
The arguments and expected behaviour of these methods are described in
Digest.
